<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rosenborg Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1606–1624</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rosenborg Castle is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> castle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a> built by Christian IV between 1606 and 1624, first as a summer house in his gardens. It was a favourite residence of the king, who died there in 1648. Since the 19th century it has been a museum of the royal collections, and it houses the Danish crown jewels.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rosenborg-castle.jpg" alt="Rosenborg Castle" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Falk2 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:I12_174_Schloss_Rosenborg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
